# Five rows in one session, on qwen2.5:7b for ten-second turns:
#
#   AC 22 - with a job scheduled, nothing schedule-shaped anywhere in .axiom/
#   AC 25 - a schedule that is not five fields is refused, and says why
#   AC 27 - a one-shot at a time that has gone is refused, and says it has passed
#   AC 17 - cancelling an identifier you invented says there is no such job
#   AC 16 - cancelling a real one is confirmed, and nothing further runs from it
#
# AC 25 and AC 27 hand the model the exact expression. That is not dodging the
# aim test: what is under test in both is axiom's *refusal*, and getting a bad
# expression as far as the tool is the precondition, not the criterion. AC 16 and
# AC 17 do make the model aim, because there the identifier is the whole point.
#
# `0 9 8 9 *` is the shape AC 27 actually needs. A daily `0 9 * * *` asked in the
# afternoon is not "a time that has gone" - it is tomorrow morning, and the code
# is right to take it. Only a fully pinned moment - minute, hour, day, month -
# names one instant in a year, which is what `_already_gone` reads.

wait: 8
send: Schedule a repeating prompt, every minute, whose text is exactly: say TICK
wait: 45
mark: === AC 22 below: a job is scheduled right now. Look at the disk ===
inspect: .axiom
mark: === AC 22 above ===

send: Schedule a prompt using exactly this cron expression, unchanged: 0 */5 * * * *  - the prompt text is: say SIX
wait: 45
mark: === AC 25 above: refused, and the refusal says what was wrong with it ===

send: Schedule a one-off prompt using exactly this cron expression, unchanged: 0 9 8 9 *  - it must run once only, and the prompt text is: say GONE
wait: 45
mark: === AC 27 above: refused, and says the time has passed ===

send: Cancel the scheduled prompt whose identifier is deadbeef.
wait: 45
mark: === AC 17 above: no such job, and nothing else changed ===

send: List everything scheduled, then cancel the TICK one using its real identifier.
wait: 60
mark: === AC 16 above: confirmed. Nothing may fire from here ===

idle: 130
mark: === AC 16: two boundaries have passed with nothing scheduled. Silence is the result ===
send: /exit
